<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37820" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-pando</span></b> , ĕre, v.
			a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to
				open</i> or <i>spread before</i>, <i>to spread out</i>, <i>extend</i> (<b>poet.</b> and in post-Aug. prose). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Verg. Cul.
			16</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vestibula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 24, 28, § 80</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: lumina menti alicujus, Lucr. 
			 1, 144: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hibernos praepandens temporis ortus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Arat. 274</span></i>
			 (40).</div>
